{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016Dr7n79AhLj9namkxEw5ni","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity + R&D mission-control system, built for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no external database â€” plain markdown is the source of truth).\n\n- **Core purpose â€” a task/project dashboard over markdown.** It reads and writes plain `.md` files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) and exposes them through an interactive web dashboard where tasks move through a lifecycle: Active â†’ Done / Cancelled / Saved-for-Later / Restored. Capture, edit, prioritize, and complete all save back to markdown automatically.\n\n- **What it ships (two interfaces, one logic).** `anchor_gui.py` is the primary app â€” a self-contained Python stdlib HTTP server that regenerates the full dashboard HTML on every request and writes directly to the markdown files. `anchor.py` mirrors the same logic as a CLI engine and generates a static `dashboard.html`. No external dependencies, Python 3.8+, with one declared exception (`pywinpty` for terminals).\n\n- **Runs as a persistent Windows service.** The server is owned by the NSSM service `anchor` (auto-start), binding `http://localhost:8777`. You don't launch it by hand; restart via `nssm restart anchor`. A daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) self-tests file integrity and every API + R&D surface (all model calls stubbed, never live).\n\n- **An R&D \"Project Cockpit\" for trio-driven development.** Beyond simple tasks, Anchor manages software projects built by the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio. Each project window is a per-lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) tile board with honest status lights; clicking a tile expands an inline panel with a cached summary plus a real, resizable ConPTY terminal (xterm.js). Launching a session \"feels like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session\" â€” the lane's skill auto-loads once, greets once.\n\n- **R&D substrate features.** Real ConPTY terminals with per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry (`.anchor/sessions.json`), proactive cached project/session summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter), stage handoffs between plan and build, an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), cost/tokens/time rollups, type-aware deliverable launch, and ephemeral deliverable previews hard-guarded off port 8777.\n\n- **Branding & scope.** Presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\" â€” but fundamentally a single-folder, single-user, markdown-backed, stdlib-only productivity and R&D orchestration system, not a multi-tenant product.\n\nThese claims are drawn from the project's own `CLAUDE.md` and frozen design docs (rnd-v2/v3/v4 master plans); the v4 \"Project Cockpit\" surface is noted as built and merged to master as of 2026-06-13."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9268eaf0-5f19-4611-b587-96c8ab46ef52","uuid":"82f1ce7a-fae1-4a76-a7b5-4b2ddb8d7e9c","request_id":"req_011Cc2MkgtbVd2sg6JhEZMp4"}
